            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0469" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/10–1744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-17T15:00:00+03:00">October 17, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3967. ReDeptel 2443, October 16, 4 p.m.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d489-f1"/> The
                    Department’s attention is drawn to Iranian press comment on Iranian Government’s
                    refusal to accept Soviet request for oil concessions in northern Iran reported
                    in immediately preceding telegram.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d489-f2"/> This
                    material appeared in <hi rendition="#italic">Pravda</hi> for October 16 and in
                    other Moscow papers for October 17. Following customary Soviet press technique
                    in such cases, the citations selected undoubtedly express the Soviet attitude
                    toward the Iranian Government’s action and are an indication of Soviet
                    dissatisfaction with the Iranian Government’s decision.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tehran.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
